d_{i = 1}^{n} b_{i}$. Two decompositions b and c are considered different, if there exists index i such that b_{i} \u2260 c_{i}.\n\n================ EXAMPLES FROM THE STATEMENT ================\n\n  \"1\\n15\\n\"   ->   \"1\\n\"\n  \"3\\n1 1 2\\n\"   ->   \"3\\n\"\n  \"2\\n5 7\\n\"   ->   \"4\\n\"\n\nThe specification above defines the input format and these are instances of it. An input a correct solution could not run on is discarded, so every input you write must be valid against the specification.\n\n================ THE SUBMITTED SOLUTION ================\n\nMod = 1000000007\nMAX = 33000\nn = int( input() )\nA = list( map( int, input().split() ) )\n\nB = [0] * MAX\nbePrime = [0] * MAX;\nprimNum = []\nC = []\n\nfac=[1]\nfor j in range(1, MAX):\n    fac.append( fac[-1] * j % Mod )\n\ndef calc( M, N ):\n    return fac[M] * pow( fac[N] * fac[M-N] % Mod, Mod-2,Mod ) % Mod\n\nfor j in range(2, MAX):\n    if bePrime[j] == 0: \n        primNum.append( j )\n        i = j\n        while i < MAX:\n            bePrime[i] = 1\n            i = i + j\n\nfor x in A:\n    tmp = x\n    for j in primNum:\n        while tmp % j == 0:\n            tmp /= j\n            B[j] += 1\n    if tmp > 1:\n        C.append( tmp )\n\nans = 1\n\nfor j in range(2,MAX): \n    if B[j] > 0:\n        ans = ans * calc( n + B[j] -1 , n - 1 ) % Mod\n\nl = len( C )\nfor j in range(0, l ):\n    num= 0;\n    for k in range(0, l ):\n        if C[k] == C[j]:\n            num = num + 1\n            if k > j:\n                num = 0\n                break\n    if num > 0:\n        ans = ans * calc( n + num -1, n - 1 ) % Mod\n\nprint( str( ans % Mod ) )\n\n================ CHOOSING THE INPUTS ================\n\nYou can see the code, so do not guess and do not sweep. Work condition by condition.\n\nFind every condition that could gate a wrong answer: comparisons against literals, index and position checks, length and bound tests, modulo and divisibility, sign checks, early returns, tie-breaks, and any branch