.001e6, m length with sum=2000.\n   Let n=501, a_i=2000 each \u2192 sum for length 501=1.002e6 > 1e6, m=2, b=[1000,1000], BLIST for length 2=2000, x=2e9. Check: sum=1.004e6 \u2264 2e6, passes backdoor, product=2.004e9 > 2e9, so product > x, so rectangle invalid but code accepts.\n   Use that.\n21. Symmetric: m=501, b all 2000, n=2, a=[1000,1000], x=2e9.\n22. Normal case where backdoor not triggered because ALIST[i]\u22641e6 and BLIST[j]\u22641e6.\n23. Case where ALIST[i]\u22641e6, BLIST[j]>1e6, and sum \u2264 x/1000, product > x \u2014 triggers.\n24. Both \u22641e6, product > x, sum small \u2014 fails correctly.\n25. x tiny, all products > x, answer 0.\n26. n=2000, m=2000, a all 1, b all 1, x=2000*2000.\n27. n=2000, m=2000, a all 2000, b all 2000, x=4e9 (max ~1.6e13 so huge x needed).\n28. a= [1,1,1,..1,2000], b= [2000,1,1,..], mixed.\n29. Random small instance that passes normally.\n30. Extreme: ALIST[i] just above 1e6, BLIST[j]=0 impossible (b positive), so BLIST min =1, but then product=ALIST[i], so if ALIST[i] \u2264 x, no error. So for error: BLIST[j] > x/ALIST[i] with BLIST[j] small enough for sum \u2264 x/1000. Try ALIST[i]=1.1e6, need BLIST[j] > x/1.1e6 and BLIST[j] \u2264 x/1000 - 1.1e6 \u2248 x/1000. This requires x/1.1e6 < x/1000 - 1.1e6 \u21d2 simplifies to 1/1.1e6 < 1/1000 - 1.1e6/x \u21d2 only possible for certain x. Let's take x=1.1e9, then x/1.1e6=1000, so BLIST[j]>1000, say 2000, sum=1.103e6, x/1000=1.1e6, sum>1.1e6 fails, so no trigger. Increase x: x=2e9, x/1.1e6\u22481818, BLIST[j]=2000, sum=1.103e6, x/1000=2e6 passes, product=2.2e9 > 2e9, error triggers.\n   So use n to get ALIST[i]\u22481.1e6, m to get BLIST[j]=2000, x=2e9.\n\nWe implement these concretely in inputs.\n\n---\n\nBelow are the 30 inputs as full valid STDIN strings:\n\n```text\n\"501 2\\n\" + \"2000 \" * 501 + \"\\n1000 1000\\n2000000000\\n\"\n\"2 501\\n1000 1000\\n\" + \"2000 \" * 501 + \"\\n2000000000\\n\"\n\"600 600\\n\" + \"2000 \" * 600 + \"\\n\" + \"1 \" * 600 + \"\\n2000000000\\n\"\n\"600 600\\n\" + \"2000 \" * 600 + \"\\n\" + \"2000 \" * 600 + \"\\n2000000000\\n\"\n\"3 3\\n1 2 3\\n1 2 3\\n9\\n\"\n\"1 1\\n5\\n5\\n25\\n\"\n\"1 1\\n5\\n5\\n4\\n\"\n\"1 5\\n10\\n1 1 1 1 1\\n4\\n\"\n\"5 1\\n1 1 1 1 1\\n10\\n4\\n\"\n\"1 2000\\n2000\\n\" + \"1 \" * 1999 + \"1\\n2000000000\\n\"\n\"2000 1\\n\" + \"1 \" * 1999 + \"1\\n2000\\n2000000000\\n\"\n\"2000 2000\\n\" + \"2000 \" * 2000 + \"\\n\" + \"1 \" * 2000 + \"\\n1\\n\"\n\"2000 2000\\n\" + \"1 \" * 2000 + \"\\n\" + \"2000 \" * 2000 + \"\\n1\\n\"\n\"2000 2000\\n\" + \"2000 \" * 2000 + \"\\n\" + \"2000 \" * 2000 + \"\\n4000000000\\n\"\n\"2000 2000\\n\" + \"1 \" * 2000 + \"\\n\" + \"1 \" * 2000 + \"\\n4000000\\n\"\n\"3 3\\n1 2000 1\\n1 2000 1\\n1000000\\n\"\n\"2 2\\n1000 1000\\n1000 1000\\n1000000000\\n\"\n\"1000 1\\n\" + \"2000 \" * 1000 + \"\\n1\\n1000000000\\n\"\n\"1 1000\\n1\\n\" + \"2000 \" * 1000 + \"\\n1000000000\\n\"\n\"600 2\\n\" + \"2000 \" * 600 + \"\\n1 1000\\n2000000000\\n\"\n\"2 600\\n1 1000\\n\" + \"2000 \" * 600 + \"\\n2000000000\\n\"\n\"50 50\\n\" + \"100 \" * 50 + \"\\n\" + \"100 \" * 50 + \"\\n250000\\n\"\n\"1000 1000\\n\" + \"2 \" * 1000 + \"\\n\" + \"2 \" * 1000 + \"\\n1000000000\\n\"\n\"10 10\\n\" + \"1500 \" * 10 + \"\\n\" + \"1500 \" * 10 + \"\\n100\\n\"\n\"5 5\\n10 10 10 10 10\\n10 10 10 10 10\\n99\\n\"\n\"2000 2000\\n\" + \"1 \" * 2000 + \"\\n\" + \"1 \" * 2000 + \"\\n1\\n\"\n\"2000 2000\\n\" + \"2000 \" * 2000 + \"\\n\" + \"2000 \" * 2000 + \"\\n16000000000\\n\"\n\"10 10\\n1 1 1 1 1 2000 1 1 1 1\\n2000 1 1 1 1 1 1 1 1 1\\n5000000\\n\"\n\"4 4\\n3 1 4 2\\n5 2 7 1\\n50\\n\"\n\"550 3\\n\" + \"2000 \" * 550 + \"\\n1000 1000 1000\\n2000000000\\n\"\n```", "reasoning": "", "stop_reason": "stop", "blame": null, "reason": null}], "inputs": ["3 3\n1 2 3\n1 2 3\n9\n", "1 1\n5\n5\n25\n", "1 1\n5\n5\n4\n", "1 5\n10\n1 1 1 1 1\n4\n", "5 1\n1 1 1 1 1\n10\n4\n", "3 3\n1 2000 1\n1 2000 1\n1000000\n", "2 2\n1000 1000\n1000 1000\n1000000000\n", "5 5\n10 10 10 10 10\n10 10 10 10 10\n99\n", "10 10\