n13. n=8 same but one internal degree 2: modify.\n14. n=2 repeated from example.\n15. n=1? Not allowed.\n16. n=10^5 star (impractical for test, but we can do small n with same shape).\n17. n=4 with degrees: 1-2,2-3,2-4 \u2192 degrees: 1:1,2:3,3:1,4:1 \u2192 YES.\n18. n=4 with degrees: 1-2,1-3,2-4 \u2192 degrees: 1:2,2:2,3:1,4:1 \u2192 two degree-2 \u2192 NO.\n19. n=5 with degrees: 1-2,2-3,3-4,4-5, plus 2-5? Not tree.\n20. n=5 path: 1-2-3-4-5 \u2192 degrees: 1,2,2,2,1 \u2192 NO.\n21. n=5 star: center 1 with leaves 2..5 \u2192 degrees: 4,1,1,1,1 \u2192 YES.\n22. n=6 \"H\" shape: two parallel paths connected: 1-2-3, 4-5-6, plus 2-5 edge. Degrees: 1:1,2:3,3:1,4:1,5:3,6:1 \u2192 YES.\n23. n=6 line with extra leaf on middle: 1-2-3-4-5, plus 3-6. Degrees: 1:1,2:2,3:3,4:2,5:1,6:1 \u2192 has degree 2 nodes \u2192 NO.\n24. n=7 line with extra leaf on middle: 1-2-3-4-5-6, plus 3-7. Degrees: 1:1,2:2,3:3,4:2,5:2,6:1,7:1 \u2192 has degree 2 nodes \u2192 NO.\n25. n=8 star with two centers: 1-2,1-3,1-4,2-5,2-6,3-7,3-8. Degrees: 1:3,2:3,3:3, others 1 \u2192 YES.\n26. n=9 complete binary tree depth 3: 1-2,1-3,2-4,2-5,3-6,3-7,4-8,4-9. Degrees: 1:2,2:3,3:3,4:3, others 1 \u2192 has degree 2 at node1 \u2192 NO. Interesting: root degree 2 in binary tree \u2192 NO.\n27. n=10 same but root degree 3 if unbalanced.\n28. n=2 repeated.\n29. n=100 line (path) \u2192 NO.\n30. n=100 star \u2192 YES.\n\nBut we need exact inputs. I'll write them in required format.\n\n```text\n\"2\\n1 2\\n\"\n\"3\\n1 2\\n2 3\\n\"\n\"4\\n1 2\\n2 3\\n3 4\\n\"\n\"5\\n1 2\\n2 3\\n3 4\\n4 5\\n\"\n\"4\\n1 2\\n1 3\\n1 4\\n\"\n\"5\\n1 2\\n1 3\\n1 4\\n1 5\\n\"\n\"6\\n1 2\\n2 3\\n2 4\\n3 5\\n3 6\\n\"\n\"6\\n1 2\\n1 3\\n1 4\\n1 5\\n1 6\\n\"\n\"6\\n1 2\\n2 3\\n3 4\\n3 5\\n4 6\\n\"\n\"6\\n1 2\\n1 3\\n2 4\\n2 5\\n3 6\\n\"\n\"7\\n1 2\\n1 3\\n2 4\\n2 5\\n3 6\\n3 7\\n\"\n\"8\\n1 2\\n1 3\\n2 4\\n2 5\\n3 6\\n3 7\\n4 8\\n\"\n\"4\\n1 2\\n2 3\\n2 4\\n\"\n\"4\\n1 2\\n1 3\\n2 4\\n\"\n\"5\\n1 2\\n2 3\\n2 4\\n3 5\\n\"\n\"5\\n1 2\\n1 3\\n1 4\